---AWS Metrics Collection resource type tag filter.
---Each filter targets either a specific AWS service's resource types (`service` and
---`resource_types`) or custom metrics (`custom`). These two modes are mutually exclusive.
---The `expression` defines a tag filter that Datadog uses when collecting metrics from the
---resource types of a specified service. Wildcards, such as `?` (match a single character)
---and `*` (match multiple characters), and exclusion using `!` before the tag are supported.
---For example, `env:production AND instance-type:c?.* AND !region:us-east-1`.
---@class datadog.v2.AWSResourceTypeTagFilter
---@field custom? boolean Whether the tag filter applies to custom metrics. When `true`, `service` and `resource_types` must be omitted.
---@field expression string The tag filter expression to apply when collecting metrics for the matching resource types.
---@field resource_types? datadog.v2.AWSResourceTypeTagFilterResourceTypesList The AWS resource types of the service to which the tag filter applies. Required when `service` is set. Use `*` as the only entry to match all resource types of the service; `*` cannot be combined with specific resource types.
---@field service? string The AWS service for which the tag filter defined in `expression` will be applied. Required unless `custom` is `true`, and must be set together with `resource_types`.

---The AWS resource types of the service to which the tag filter applies. Required when `service` is set. Use `*` as the only entry to match all resource types of the service; `*` cannot be combined with specific resource types.
