---Visible request filters. Provider and model tags are withheld when the caller cannot view them. An empty object or empty tags can represent a fully restricted scope; scope_restricted identifies redaction.
---@class datadog.v2.AiGatewayCaptureResponseScope
---@field tags? datadog.v2.AiGatewayCaptureResponseScopeTagsMap Exact-match request tags with lowercase keys. The reserved `model` tag is the canonical model ID, and the reserved `provider` tag is the configured connection slug. The server sets both. Custom tags come from `x-dd-tag` headers. Keys and values must not have leading or trailing white space. Values are case-sensitive.
---@field team_id? string UUID of a Datadog team. Matches the authorized team selected by the `x-ai-gateway-team` request header. Requests without this header do not match team-scoped overrides. Open-membership teams cannot scope overrides.
