---A configurable argument of a forwarded static analysis rule.
---@class datadog.v2.AnalysisRequestRuleArgument
---@field description? string An explanation of the argument's purpose and accepted values.
---@field name? string The name of the rule argument.

---A static analysis rule to apply during code analysis. Clients forward complete rule
---objects returned by the rulesets endpoints, so every member of that resource is
---declared here; only `id`, `category`, `checksum`, `language`, `severity`,
---`tree_sitter_query`, `entity_checked`, `regex`, `type` and `code` are read by this
---operation and the rest are ignored. The schema stays open so that any member beyond
---the forwarded rule resource is reported as a promotion candidate rather than
---rejected; it can be closed once that telemetry confirms none remain.
---@class datadog.v2.AnalysisRequestRuleInput
---@field arguments? datadog.v2.AnalysisRequestRuleInputArgumentsList The configurable arguments accepted by the rule. Forwarded from the rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field category string The category of the rule (for example, `BEST_PRACTICES`, `SECURITY`).
---@field checksum string A checksum of the rule definition.
---@field code string The base64-encoded rule implementation code.
---@field creation_message? string The message associated with the custom rule revision. Forwarded from the custom rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field cve? string The CVE identifier associated with the rule. Forwarded from the rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field cwe? string The CWE identifier associated with the rule. Forwarded from the rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field description? string A detailed explanation of what the rule detects. Forwarded from the rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field documentation_url? string A URL pointing to the rule documentation. Forwarded from the rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field entity_checked? string|distilled.Null The code entity type checked by the rule, applicable when rule type is `AST_CHECK`.
---@field id string The unique identifier of the rule.
---@field is_published? boolean Whether the rule is published. Forwarded from the rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field is_testing? boolean Whether the rule is in testing mode. Forwarded from the rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field language string The programming language this rule targets.
---@field name? string The name of the rule. Forwarded from the rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field regex? string|distilled.Null A base64-encoded regex pattern used by the rule, applicable when rule type is `REGEX`.
---@field severity string The severity of findings from this rule (for example, `ERROR`, `WARNING`).
---@field short_description? string A brief summary of what the rule detects. Forwarded from the rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field should_use_ai_fix? boolean Whether an AI-generated fix should be offered. Forwarded from the rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field tags? datadog.v2.AnalysisRequestRuleInputTagsList Tags associated with the custom rule revision. Forwarded from the custom rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field tests? datadog.v2.AnalysisRequestRuleInputTestsList The test cases associated with the rule. Forwarded from the rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field tree_sitter_query string The base64-encoded tree-sitter query used by the rule.
---@field type string The rule type indicating the detection mechanism (for example, `TREE_SITTER_QUERY`).
---@field version_id? number The custom rule revision version. Forwarded from the custom rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@field [string] any

---The configurable arguments accepted by the rule. Forwarded from the rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@alias datadog.v2.AnalysisRequestRuleInputArgumentsList datadog.v2.AnalysisRequestRuleArgument[]

---Tags associated with the custom rule revision. Forwarded from the custom rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
---@alias datadog.v2.AnalysisRequestRuleInputTagsList string[]

---The test cases associated with the rule. Forwarded from the rulesets endpoints; ignored by this operation.
