---@class datadog.v2.CountSecurityAgentInvestigationsRequest
---@field field datadog.v2.SecurityAgentInvestigationCountField|string Field to count completed investigations by.
---@field filter_title_? string Only investigations whose signal title contains this text, case-insensitive.
---@field filter_from_? string Only investigations last updated at or after this time, as RFC 3339 or milliseconds since the epoch.
---@field filter_to_? string Only investigations last updated at or before this time, as RFC 3339 or milliseconds since the epoch.
---@field filter_verdict_? string Only investigations with one of these verdicts: `benign`, `suspicious`, or `malicious`. Comma-separated values; an investigation matches any of them.
---@field filter_rule_id_? string Only investigations of signals from one of these detection rule IDs. Comma-separated values; an investigation matches any of them.
---@field filter_rule_type_? string Only investigations of signals from detection rules of one of these types, as returned by the count with `field=rule_type`. Comma-separated values; an investigation matches any of them.
---@field filter_signal_severity_? string Only investigations of signals with one of these severities: `info`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, or `critical`. Comma-separated values; an investigation matches any of them.
---@field filter_signal_source_? string Only investigations of signals from one of these sources, as returned by the count with `field=signal_source`. Comma-separated values; an investigation matches any of them.
---@field filter_tags_? string Only investigations whose signal has all of these tags, written `key:value`. Comma-separated values; an investigation must have every one of them.
---@field filter_entity_? string Only investigations whose signal has all of these entities. Write each entity as `attribute:value`, matching the values returned by the count endpoint with `field=entity`. Comma-separated values; an investigation must have every one of them.

