---The Elasticsearch destination.
---@class datadog.v2.CustomDestinationForwardDestinationElasticsearch
---@field auth datadog.v2.CustomDestinationElasticsearchDestinationAuth
---@field endpoint string The destination for which logs will be forwarded to. Must have HTTPS scheme and forwarding back to Datadog is not allowed.
---@field index_name string Name of the Elasticsearch index (must follow [Elasticsearch's criteria](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/8.11/indices-create-index.html#indices-create-api-path-params)).
---@field index_rotation? string Date pattern with US locale and UTC timezone to be appended to the index name after adding `-` (that is, `${index_name}-${indexPattern}`). You can customize the index rotation naming pattern by choosing one of these options: - Hourly: `yyyy-MM-dd-HH` (as an example, it would render: `2022-10-19-09`) - Daily: `yyyy-MM-dd` (as an example, it would render: `2022-10-19`) - Weekly: `yyyy-'W'ww` (as an example, it would render: `2022-W42`) - Monthly: `yyyy-MM` (as an example, it would render: `2022-10`) If this field is missing or is blank, it means that the index name will always be the same (that is, no rotation).
---@field type datadog.v2.CustomDestinationForwardDestinationElasticsearchType|string

