---Deletion attribute for data deletion response.
---@class datadog.v2.DataDeletionResponseItemAttributes
---@field created_at string Creation time of the deletion request.
---@field created_by string User who created the deletion request.
---@field customer_message? string A message for the customer regarding the deletion request, if any.
---@field displayed_total number Total number of elements to be deleted as displayed to the user.
---@field error_category? string The category of the error for the deletion request, if any.
---@field from_time number Start of requested time window, milliseconds since Unix epoch.
---@field indexes? datadog.v2.DataDeletionResponseItemAttributesIndexesList List of indexes for the search. If not provided, the search is performed in all indexes.
---@field is_created boolean Whether the deletion request is fully created or not. It can take several minutes to fully create a deletion request depending on the target query and timeframe.
---@field org_id number Organization ID.
---@field product string Product name.
---@field query string Query for creating a data deletion request.
---@field recoverable_until? string Time when the recovery period for the deletion request ends. Before this time, you can cancel the request and recover the data. After this time, permanent deletion begins, and the status changes to `deleting` within a few minutes. This field is returned only for `in_progress` requests when listing deletion requests, and is omitted if the value cannot be determined.
---@field source? string The source of the deletion request.
---@field starting_at string Starting time of the process to delete the requested data.
---@field status string Status of the deletion request.
---@field to_time number End of requested time window, milliseconds since Unix epoch.
---@field total_unrestricted number Total number of elements to be deleted. Only the data accessible to the current user that matches the query and timeframe provided will be deleted.
---@field updated_at string Update time of the deletion request.

---List of indexes for the search. If not provided, the search is performed in all indexes.
