---A test service is a group of tests associated with a project or repository. It contains all the individual tests for your code, optionally organized into test suites, which are like folders for your tests.
---@alias datadog.v2.FlakyTestAttributesServicesList string[]

---A single history entry representing a status change for a flaky test.
---@class datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistory
---@field commit_sha string The commit SHA associated with this status change. Will be an empty string if the commit SHA is not available.
---@field policy_id? datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistoryPolicyId
---@field policy_meta? datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistoryPolicyMeta|distilled.Null
---@field status string The test status at this point in history.
---@field timestamp number Unix timestamp in milliseconds when this status change occurred.

---The policy that triggered this status change.
---@alias datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistoryPolicyId "ftm_policy.manual"|"ftm_policy.fixed"|"ftm_policy.disable.failure_rate"|"ftm_policy.disable.branch_flake"|"ftm_policy.disable.days_active"|"ftm_policy.quarantine.failure_rate"|"ftm_policy.quarantine.branch_flake"|"ftm_policy.quarantine.days_active"|"unknown"

---Metadata about the policy that triggered this status change.
---@class datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistoryPolicyMeta
---@field branches? datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistoryPolicyMetaBranchesList|distilled.Null Branches where the test was flaky at the time of the status change.
---@field config? datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistoryPolicyMetaConfig|distilled.Null
---@field days_active? number|distilled.Null The number of days the test has been active at the time of the status change.
---@field days_without_flake? number|distilled.Null The number of days since the test last exhibited flakiness.
---@field failure_rate? number|distilled.Null The failure rate of the test at the time of the status change.
---@field state? string|distilled.Null The previous state of the test.
---@field total_runs? number|distilled.Null The total number of test runs at the time of the status change.

---Branches where the test was flaky at the time of the status change.
---@alias datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistoryPolicyMetaBranchesList string[]

---Configuration parameters of the policy that triggered this status change.
---@class datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistoryPolicyMetaConfig
---@field branches? datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistoryPolicyMetaConfigBranchesList|distilled.Null The branches considered by the policy.
---@field days_active? number|distilled.Null The number of days a test must have been active for the policy to trigger.
---@field failure_rate? number|distilled.Null The failure rate threshold for the policy to trigger.
---@field forget_branches? datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistoryPolicyMetaConfigForgetBranchesList|distilled.Null Branches excluded from the policy evaluation.
---@field required_runs? number|distilled.Null The minimum number of test runs required for the policy to trigger.
---@field state? string|distilled.Null The target state the policy transitions the test from.
---@field test_services? datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistoryPolicyMetaConfigTestServicesList|distilled.Null Test services excluded from the policy evaluation.

---The branches considered by the policy.
---@alias datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistoryPolicyMetaConfigBranchesList string[]

---Branches excluded from the policy evaluation.
---@alias datadog.v2.FlakyTestHistoryPolicyMetaConfigForgetBranchesList string[]

