---Attributes associated with your service account.
---@class datadog.v2.GCPSTSServiceAccountAttributes
---@field account_tags? datadog.v2.GCPSTSServiceAccountAttributesAccountTagsList Tags to be associated with GCP metrics and service checks from your account.
---@field automute? boolean Silence monitors for expected GCE instance shutdowns.
---@field client_email? string Your service account email address.
---@field cloud_run_revision_filters? datadog.v2.GCPSTSServiceAccountAttributesCloudRunRevisionFiltersList List of filters to limit the Cloud Run revisions that are pulled into Datadog by using tags. Only Cloud Run revision resources that apply to specified filters are imported into Datadog. **Note:** This field is deprecated. Instead, use `monitored_resource_configs` with `type=cloud_run_revision`
---@field host_filters? datadog.v2.GCPSTSServiceAccountAttributesHostFiltersList List of filters to limit the VM instances that are pulled into Datadog by using tags. Only VM instance resources that apply to specified filters are imported into Datadog. **Note:** This field is deprecated. Instead, use `monitored_resource_configs` with `type=gce_instance`
---@field is_cspm_enabled? boolean When enabled, Datadog will activate the Cloud Security Monitoring product for this service account. Note: This requires resource_collection_enabled or is_org_folder_resource_collection_enabled to be set to true.
---@field is_global_location_enabled? boolean When enabled, Datadog collects metrics where location is explicitly stated as "global" or where location information cannot be deduced from GCP labels.
---@field is_org_folder_resource_collection_enabled? boolean When enabled, Datadog scans for organization and folder-level resources under the organization the service account belongs to.
---@field is_per_project_quota_enabled? boolean When enabled, Datadog applies the `X-Goog-User-Project` header, attributing Google Cloud billing and quota usage to the project being monitored rather than the default service account project.
---@field is_resource_change_collection_enabled? boolean When enabled, Datadog scans for all resource change data in your Google Cloud environment.
---@field is_security_command_center_enabled? boolean When enabled, Datadog will attempt to collect Security Command Center Findings. Note: This requires additional permissions on the service account.
---@field metric_namespace_configs? datadog.v2.GCPSTSServiceAccountAttributesMetricNamespaceConfigsList Configurations for GCP metric namespaces.
---@field monitored_resource_configs? datadog.v2.GCPSTSServiceAccountAttributesMonitoredResourceConfigsList Configurations for GCP monitored resources.
---@field region_filter_configs? datadog.v2.GCPSTSServiceAccountAttributesRegionFilterConfigsList Configurations for GCP location filtering, such as region, multi-region, or zone. Only monitored resources that match the specified regions are imported into Datadog. By default, Datadog collects from all locations.
