---@class datadog.v2.GetAggregatedConnectionsRequest
---@field from? number Unix timestamp (number of seconds since epoch) of the start of the query window. If not provided, the start of the query window is 15 minutes before the `to` timestamp. If neither `from` nor `to` are provided, the query window is `[now - 15m, now]`.
---@field to? number Unix timestamp (number of seconds since epoch) of the end of the query window. If not provided, the end of the query window is the current time. If neither `from` nor `to` are provided, the query window is `[now - 15m, now]`.
---@field group_by? string Comma-separated list of fields to group connections by. The maximum number of group_by(s) is 10.
---@field tags? string Comma-separated list of tags to filter connections by.
---@field query? string Free-form search query using AND/OR/NOT operators, wildcards, and parentheses. When provided, takes precedence over the `tags` parameter.
---@field limit? number The number of connections to be returned. The maximum value is 7500. The default is 100.

---@class datadog.v2.GetAggregatedDnsRequest
---@field from? number Unix timestamp (number of seconds since epoch) of the start of the query window. If not provided, the start of the query window is 15 minutes before the `to` timestamp. If neither `from` nor `to` are provided, the query window is `[now - 15m, now]`.
---@field to? number Unix timestamp (number of seconds since epoch) of the end of the query window. If not provided, the end of the query window is the current time. If neither `from` nor `to` are provided, the query window is `[now - 15m, now]`.
---@field group_by? string Comma-separated list of fields to group DNS traffic by. The server side defaults to `network.dns_query` if unspecified. `server_ungrouped` may be used if groups are not desired. The maximum number of group_by(s) is 10.
---@field tags? string Comma-separated list of tags to filter DNS traffic by.
---@field query? string Free-form search query using AND/OR/NOT operators, wildcards, and parentheses. When provided, takes precedence over the `tags` parameter.
---@field limit? number The number of aggregated DNS entries to be returned. The maximum value is 7500. The default is 100.

