---LLM judge configuration for a custom evaluator.
---@class datadog.v2.LLMObsCustomEvalConfigLLMJudgeConfig
---@field assessment_criteria? datadog.v2.LLMObsCustomEvalConfigAssessmentCriteria
---@field context_query? string|distilled.Null Query used to extract additional context for the evaluation.
---@field inference_params datadog.v2.LLMObsCustomEvalConfigInferenceParams
---@field last_used_library_prompt_template_name? string|distilled.Null Name of the last library prompt template used.
---@field modified_library_prompt_template? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the library prompt template was modified.
---@field output_schema? datadog.v2.LLMObsCustomEvalConfigLLMJudgeConfigOutputSchemaMap|distilled.Null JSON schema describing the expected output format of the LLM judge. Omit for a `deterministic` evaluator.
---@field parsing_type? datadog.v2.LLMObsCustomEvalConfigParsingType|string
---@field prompt_template? datadog.v2.LLMObsCustomEvalConfigLLMJudgeConfigPromptTemplateList List of messages forming the LLM judge prompt template. Omit for a `deterministic` evaluator.
---@field target_query? string|distilled.Null Query used to extract the target value to evaluate.
---@field user_specified_json_post_processing_function? string|distilled.Null User-provided JavaScript function applied to post-process the JSON output of the LLM judge. For a `deterministic` evaluator it is the evaluator itself: it receives the evaluated span (span scope), `{spans}` (trace scope), or `{session_id, traces}` (session scope), and its return value sets the result. A boolean, number, string or object becomes a boolean, score, categorical or JSON metric; `null` skips the evaluation; and `{value, assessment, reasoning, metadata}` also sets pass or fail, reasoning, and metadata.

