---@class datadog.v2.ListAiGatewayBudgetInstanceDimensionsRequest
---@field id string Budget UUID.
---@field window? string RFC3339 timestamp inside the desired accounting window. Omit to use the current window.
---@field split_dim? datadog.v2.ListAiGatewayBudgetInstanceDimensionsRequestSplitDimList Keep only instance counters whose split dimension equals a value, written as `<dim>=<value>`, such as `split_dim=user_id=<uuid>&split_dim=tag:env=prod`. Dimensions use the `split_dims` names `user_id`, `team_id`, `model`, `provider`, and `tag:<key>`. Repeat the parameter to filter on several dimensions; a counter must match all of them. Each dimension may appear once and must be a per-value dimension of the budget.
---@field dim? datadog.v2.ListAiGatewayBudgetInstanceDimensionsRequestDimList Return only these split dimensions, such as `dim=user_id`. Repeat the parameter for several dimensions. Omit it to return every split dimension of the budget.
---@field query? string Keep only values that contain this text, case-insensitively. It matches raw values, so User and Team values match their UUIDs; search their names elsewhere and pass the IDs as `value`.
---@field value? datadog.v2.ListAiGatewayBudgetInstanceDimensionsRequestValueList Keep only these values. Repeat the parameter to check several candidates, such as User IDs found by name, and learn which of them have instance counters.
---@field limit? number Maximum number of values to return per dimension.

---@alias datadog.v2.ListAiGatewayBudgetInstanceDimensionsRequestDimList string[]

---@alias datadog.v2.ListAiGatewayBudgetInstanceDimensionsRequestSplitDimList string[]

---@alias datadog.v2.ListAiGatewayBudgetInstanceDimensionsRequestValueList string[]

