---@class datadog.v2.ListContainerImagesRequest
---@field filter_tags_? string Comma-separated `key:value` tags. An image must match every tag. Wildcards, negation (`-key:value`), spaces, and `IN (...)` are not supported. Use keys such as `image_registry` and `image_tag`. To match any of several values of the same key, make one request per value.
---@field group_by? string Comma-separated list of up to three tag keys, such as `image_registry,image_tag`. Returns `container_image_group` objects with counts and tags. Grouped results ignore `sort` and do not support pagination. Images missing a grouping key are excluded. An image with multiple values for a grouping tag can appear in multiple groups. Grouped results may be incomplete. Compare counts only within the returned groups; they do not establish the most common tags or proportions across the inventory. For inventory-wide comparisons, omit `group_by`, keep the same filters, paginate all results, and deduplicate by returned image ID. For an inventory total, use `meta.pagination.total` from a query without grouping.
---@field sort? string Attribute to sort individual images by, such as `size` or `container_count`. Defaults to `image_name` in ascending order. Prefix the attribute with `-` for descending order, such as `-size`. Ignored when `group_by` is specified.
---@field page_size_? number Maximum number of results returned. Grouped queries default to `100`, with a maximum of `1000` groups. Without grouping, queries default to `1000`, with a maximum of `10000` images. Minimum is `1`.
---@field page_cursor_? string Opaque cursor from `meta.pagination.next_cursor` for individual images. Keep the same filters and sort order. Stop when absent or empty. Grouped queries do not support pagination.

---@class datadog.v2.ListContainersRequest
---@field filter_tags_? string Comma-separated `key:value` tags. A container must match every tag. Wildcards, negation (`-key:value`), spaces, and `IN (...)` are not supported. To cover several hosts, make one request per host.
---@field group_by? string Comma-separated list of up to three tag keys to group containers by. Returns `container_group` objects with counts and tags. Grouped results ignore `sort` and do not support pagination. Containers with multiple values for a grouping tag can appear in multiple groups. Summing group counts can overcount distinct containers.
---@field sort? string Attribute to sort individual containers by: `name`, `created_at`, `started_at`, `state`, `container_id`, `host`, `image_name`, or `image_digest`. Defaults to `started_at` in ascending order. Prefix the attribute with `-` for descending order, such as `-started_at`. Ignored when `group_by` is specified.
---@field page_size_? number Maximum number of results returned. For grouped results, defaults to `100` with a maximum of `1000` groups.
---@field page_cursor_? string String to query the next page of results. This key is provided with each valid response from the API in `meta.pagination.next_cursor`.

---@class datadog.v2.ListCostAWSCURConfigsRequest

---@class datadog.v2.ListCostAnomaliesRequest
---@field start? number Start time as Unix milliseconds. Defaults to the start of the latest stable seven-day window.
---@field ["end"]? number End time as Unix milliseconds. Defaults to the end of the latest stable seven-day window.
---@field filter? string Optional JSON object mapping cost tag keys to allowed values, for example `{"team":["payments"],"env":["prod"]}`. Filters match anomaly dimensions or correlated tags.
---@field min_anomalous_threshold? string Minimum absolute anomalous cost change to include. Numeric value; defaults to `1`.
---@field min_cost_threshold? string Minimum absolute actual cost to include. Numeric value; defaults to `0`.
---@field dismissal_cause? string Filter by resolution state. Use `none` for unresolved anomalies, `all` or `*` for resolved anomalies, or a comma-separated list of causes.
---@field order_by? string Sort field. One of `start_date`, `end_date`, `duration`, `max_cost`, `anomalous_cost`, or `dismissal_date`. Defaults to `anomalous_cost`.
---@field order? string Sort direction. One of `asc` or `desc`. Defaults to `desc`.
---@field limit? number Maximum number of anomalies to return. Defaults to `200`.
---@field offset? number Pagination offset. Defaults to `0`.
---@field provider_ids? datadog.v2.ListCostAnomaliesRequestProviderIdsList Optional repeated cloud or SaaS provider filters, such as `aws`, `gcp`, `azure`, `Oracle`, `datadog`, `OpenAI`, or `Anthropic`.

---@alias datadog.v2.ListCostAnomaliesRequestProviderIdsList string[]

