---@class datadog.v2.ListFeatureFlagsRequest
---@field key? string Filter feature flags by an exact, case-sensitive key. Use `search` for partial matching.
---@field is_archived? boolean Filter by archived status. If `true`, return only archived flags. If `false`, return only flags that are not archived. If omitted, return both.
---@field limit? number Deprecated alias for `page[limit]`. Use `page[limit]` for new requests. Used only when `page[limit]` is absent. When both parameters are omitted, the server defaults to `25`. Values that exceed `50` are set to `50`; non-positive or empty values use the server default.
---@field offset? number Deprecated alias for `page[offset]`. Used only when `page[offset]` is absent. Defaults to `0`. Negative or empty values are set to `0`.
---@field tags? datadog.v2.ListFeatureFlagsRequestTagsList Filter by exact tag values using repeated parameters, such as `tags=env:prod&tags=purpose:sitemap`. A flag must have all ordinary tags. Values of the form `team:<handle>` match any selected team and are combined with `teams` into one set. The result must match all ordinary tags, any selected team, and all other filters. Empty values are ignored.
---@field teams? datadog.v2.ListFeatureFlagsRequestTeamsList Filter by team handles without the `team:` prefix. Use repeated parameters to filter by multiple team handles, such as `teams=checkout&teams=payments`. A flag must belong to at least one selected team. Team handles from `teams` and `team:<handle>` values from tags are treated as a single set and combined with ordinary tags and other filters using AND logic. Duplicate handles do not duplicate results. Unknown handles do not match any flags. Empty handles, surrounding white space, or using the `team:` prefix return a bad request error. Response tags are unchanged.
---@field production_status? datadog.v2.ListFeatureFlagsRequestProductionStatusList Filter by status across production environments. Use repeated parameters to match any selected status. `ENABLED` matches at least one enabled production environment without a variant override. `OVERRIDDEN` matches at least one enabled production environment with a variant override. `DISABLED` matches flags whose associated production environments are all disabled. A flag can match both `ENABLED` and `OVERRIDDEN` in different environments. Flags without associated production environments do not match. This does not filter by a specific environment. Unknown values do not match any status.
---@field distribution_channel? datadog.v2.FeatureFlagDistributionChannel|string Filter by SDK availability. `CLIENT` returns flags with channel `CLIENT` or `ALL`. `SERVER` returns flags with channel `SERVER` or `ALL`. `ALL`, an empty value, or omission applies no channel restriction; it does not select only flags whose channel is `ALL`. Values are case-insensitive and surrounding white space is ignored. Invalid values return a bad request error.
---@field search? string Case-insensitive substring search on flag names, keys, and tag names. Combined with all other filters. An empty value applies no search restriction.
---@field value_type? datadog.v2.ListFeatureFlagsRequestValueTypeList Filter by variant value types using repeated parameters. A flag must match at least one selected type. Empty values are ignored. Invalid types return a bad request error.
---@field created_by? datadog.v2.ListFeatureFlagsRequestCreatedByList Filter by creator UUIDs using repeated parameters. A flag must match at least one creator. Empty values are ignored. Invalid UUIDs return a bad request error.
---@field flag_ids? datadog.v2.ListFeatureFlagsRequestFlagIdsList Filter by feature flag UUIDs using repeated parameters. A flag must match at least one ID and all other filters. Duplicate IDs return each flag once. Unknown IDs and IDs from other organizations do not match any flags. Empty or invalid UUIDs return a bad request error. Pagination still applies.
---@field staleness_status? datadog.v2.FeatureFlagStalenessStatus|string Filter by the computed staleness status: `ACTIVE`, `STALE`, or `PERMANENT`. Values are case-insensitive and surrounding white space is ignored. An empty value or omission applies no restriction. Invalid values return a bad request error. Read the computed result from `staleness_details.staleness_status`, not the legacy `staleness_status` response field.
---@field saved_filter_id? string Filter to flags that reference this saved filter in their targeting conditions. An empty value or omission applies no restriction. An invalid UUID returns a bad request error.
---@field sort? string Sort by `name`, `updated_at`, `created_at`, or `evaluations`. Use a comma-separated list for multiple sort fields and prefix a field with `-` for descending order. The default is `updated_at` descending. When favorites are enabled, the authenticated user's favorite flags take precedence over the selected ordering. Unknown fields return a bad request error.
---@field page_limit_? number Maximum number of flags to return. Defaults to `25` and is capped at `50`. Values that exceed `50` are set to `50`. Non-positive or empty values use the default. A non-integer value returns a bad request error. Takes precedence over `limit` when both are present. Pagination applies even when no pagination parameters are supplied.
---@field page_offset_? number Number of matching flags to skip before returning results. Defaults to `0`. Negative or empty values are set to `0`. A non-integer value returns a bad request error. Takes precedence over `offset` when both are present.

---@alias datadog.v2.ListFeatureFlagsRequestCreatedByList string[]

