---The `spike_protection` processor learns the normal ingestion volume for the logs that match a specified filter and takes action when the volume spikes unexpectedly.
---
---**Supported pipeline types:** logs
---@class datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessor
---@field action_when_missing_partitions? datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorActionWhenMissingPartitions|string
---@field display_name? string
---@field enabled boolean Indicates whether the processor is enabled.
---@field id string The unique identifier for this component. Used in other parts of the pipeline to reference this component (for example, as the `input` to downstream components).
---@field include string A Datadog search query used to determine which logs this processor targets.
---@field minimal_threshold? number The minimum volume, in bytes, that must be observed within 24 hours before spike protection can activate. Defaults to 100 GiB.
---@field minimal_threshold_overrides? datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorMinimalThresholdOverridesList A list of per-partition overrides for the minimal threshold, identified by matching field values. Requires `partition_fields` to be set.
---@field name string Name of the spike protection rule.
---@field partition_fields? datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorPartitionFieldsList A list of fields used to segment log traffic. Volume is learned and evaluated independently for each unique combination of these field values. A maximum of five fields is supported.
---@field spike_action datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorSpikeAction|string
---@field spike_threshold? number The number of standard deviations above the learned mean volume that must be exceeded before a spike is detected. Defaults to `5`.
---@field type datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorType|string

---How to handle logs that are missing one of the `partition_fields`. Options:
---- `ignore`: Forward the event without applying spike protection.
---- `default_bucket`: Assign the event to a default partition.
---@alias datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorActionWhenMissingPartitions "ignore"|"default_bucket"

---The minimal threshold to apply to the matching partition.
---@alias datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorMinimalThreshold datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorMinimalThresholdBytes|datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorMinimalThresholdAlwaysKeep

---Never activates spike protection for the matching partition, regardless of volume.
---@class datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorMinimalThresholdAlwaysKeep
---@field type datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorMinimalThresholdAlwaysKeepType|string

---The minimal threshold type. The value should always be `always_keep`.
---@alias datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorMinimalThresholdAlwaysKeepType "always_keep"

---Sets a specific byte threshold for the matching partition.
---@class datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorMinimalThresholdBytes
---@field bytes number The minimal threshold, in bytes, for the matching partition.
---@field type datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorMinimalThresholdBytesType|string

---The minimal threshold type. The value should always be `threshold`.
---@alias datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorMinimalThresholdBytesType "threshold"

---A list of per-partition overrides for the minimal threshold, identified by matching field values. Requires `partition_fields` to be set.
---@alias datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorMinimalThresholdOverridesList datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorThresholdOverride[]

---A list of fields used to segment log traffic. Volume is learned and evaluated independently for each unique combination of these field values. A maximum of five fields is supported.
---@alias datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorPartitionFieldsList string[]

---The action to take with matching logs while spike protection is active. Options:
---- `drop`: Drop the event.
---- `no_action`: Let the event pass through.
---- `overflow_routing`: Route to an overflow destination.
---
---When `overflow_routing` is used, there must be a destination whose `inputs` reference this processor with the `<processor-id>.overflow_events` suffix to route the overflowing events.
---@alias datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorSpikeAction "drop"|"no_action"|"overflow_routing"

---Defines a minimal threshold that applies to a specific partition instead of the processor-wide `minimal_threshold`.
---@class datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorThresholdOverride
---@field fields datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorThresholdOverrideFieldsList The set of field matchers that identifies the partition this override applies to. Every field name listed must also appear in `partition_fields`.
---@field minimal_threshold datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorMinimalThreshold

---The set of field matchers that identifies the partition this override applies to. Every field name listed must also appear in `partition_fields`.
---@alias datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorThresholdOverrideFieldsList datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineFieldValue[]

---The processor type. The value should always be `spike_protection`.
---@alias datadog.v2.ObservabilityPipelineSpikeProtectionProcessorType "spike_protection"

