---@field monthly_quantity number The quantity allotted per month.
---@field parent_sku_code string The code of the SKU that provides the allotment. Always the code of the SKU the allotment is returned under.

---The pricing and allotment metadata of a SKU.
---@class datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUDataAttributesResponse
---@field allotments datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUDataAttributesResponseAllotmentsList The allotments the SKU provides to other SKUs. Every entry carries the code of this SKU as its `parent_sku_code`. Empty when the SKU provides no allotments.
---@field billing_dimension string The identifier of the billing dimension the SKU is billed on, as used by the usage metering endpoints. Several SKUs can share one billing dimension, so this value does not identify a SKU.
---@field billing_units string|distilled.Null The billable usage unit the SKU is priced per. `null` for SKUs that are not priced per unit of usage, such as those whose `pricing_type` is `percent`.
---@field currency string The ISO-4217 code of the currency the prices are expressed in.
---@field default_on_demand_option datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUOnDemandOption
---@field number_of_units_included_in_price number The number of billable usage units that one unit of price covers. Divide measured usage by this value before multiplying by the price. For example, a SKU priced at `18.00` with `number_of_units_included_in_price` of `1` costs `18.00` per host, while a SKU priced at `12.00` with `number_of_units_included_in_price` of `10000` costs `12.00` per 10,000 requests. It is a scaling factor on the price, not a free allotment; included quantities are in `allotments`. The same factor applies to the price of a tier in `on_demand_tiered` whose `pricing_unit_type` is `unit`. It does not apply to a tier whose `pricing_unit_type` is `block`: that tier's `price` is charged for the whole block bounded by `min_usage_quantity` and `max_usage_quantity`, however much of the block is used. `0` for SKUs that are not priced per unit of usage, such as those whose `pricing_type` is `percent`.
---@field on_demand_list_price string|distilled.Null The public list price of on-demand usage of the SKU, as a decimal string. The number of decimal places is not normalized, so values such as `0`, `0.9`, and `30000.00` all occur. `null` when the SKU is priced with tiers, in which case the prices are in `on_demand_tiered`.
---@field on_demand_tiered datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUTieredPricing|distilled.Null
---@field pricing_type datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUPricingType
---@field sku_name string The human-readable name of the SKU.

---The allotments the SKU provides to other SKUs. Every entry carries the code of this
---SKU as its `parent_sku_code`. Empty when the SKU provides no allotments.
---@alias datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUDataAttributesResponseAllotmentsList datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUAllotment[]

---A SKU and the pricing metadata that applies to it.
---@class datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUDataResponse
---@field attributes datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUDataAttributesResponse
---@field id string The code that identifies the SKU.
---@field type datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUType

---The billing frequency applied to on-demand usage of the SKU by default.
---@alias datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUOnDemandOption "hourly"|"monthly"

---A usage range and the price that applies to usage falling inside it.
---@class datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUPricingTier
---@field max_usage_quantity number|distilled.Null The exclusive upper bound of the usage range the tier prices. `null` on the final tier, which is unbounded.
---@field min_usage_quantity number The inclusive lower bound of the usage range the tier prices.
---@field price string The price applied to usage in the tier, as a decimal string. The number of decimal places is not normalized, so free tiers appear as either `0` or `0.00`.
---@field pricing_unit_type datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUPricingUnitType

---How the SKU is priced. `usage` prices each billable usage unit, and `percent` prices a
---percentage; percent-priced SKUs have no `billing_units`.
---@alias datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUPricingType "usage"|"percent"

---Whether the tier's price applies per unit of usage or to a block of usage.
---@alias datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUPricingUnitType "block"|"unit"

---The tiered pricing applied to on-demand usage of the SKU. `null` when the SKU is priced
---with a single list price instead.
---@class datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUTieredPricing
---@field tiers datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUTieredPricingTiersList The pricing tiers, ordered by ascending usage quantity.

---The pricing tiers, ordered by ascending usage quantity.
---@alias datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUTieredPricingTiersList datadog.v2.ProductCatalogSKUPricingTier[]

