---@field type? datadog.v2.SensitiveDataScannerStandardPatternType

---Object describing suppressions for a rule, or the recommended suppression lists published by a standard pattern.
---There are three types of suppressions, `starts_with`, `ends_with`, and `exact_match`.
---Rules based on the Datadog library can use recommended or custom suppressions. Custom rules can only use custom suppressions.
---Suppressed matches are not obfuscated, counted in metrics, or displayed in the Findings page.
---@class datadog.v2.SensitiveDataScannerSuppressions
---@field ends_with? datadog.v2.SensitiveDataScannerSuppressionsEndsWithList List of strings to use for suppression of matches ending with these strings.
---@field exact_match? datadog.v2.SensitiveDataScannerSuppressionsExactMatchList List of strings to use for suppression of matches exactly matching these strings.
---@field starts_with? datadog.v2.SensitiveDataScannerSuppressionsStartsWithList List of strings to use for suppression of matches starting with these strings.
---@field use_recommended_suppressions? boolean Should the rule use the underlying standard pattern suppression configuration. If set to `true`, the rule must be tied to a standard pattern. If set to `false`, the specified suppressions are applied.

---List of strings to use for suppression of matches ending with these strings.
---@alias datadog.v2.SensitiveDataScannerSuppressionsEndsWithList string[]

---List of strings to use for suppression of matches exactly matching these strings.
---@alias datadog.v2.SensitiveDataScannerSuppressionsExactMatchList string[]

---List of strings to use for suppression of matches starting with these strings.
---@alias datadog.v2.SensitiveDataScannerSuppressionsStartsWithList string[]

---Object describing how the scanned event will be replaced.
---@class datadog.v2.SensitiveDataScannerTextReplacement
---@field number_of_chars? number Required if type == 'partial_replacement_from_beginning' or 'partial_replacement_from_end'. It must be > 0.
---@field replacement_string? string Required if type == 'replacement_string'.
---@field should_save_match? boolean Only valid when type == `replacement_string`. When enabled, matches can be unmasked in logs by users with ‘Data Scanner Unmask’ permission. As a security best practice, avoid masking for highly-sensitive, long-lived data.
---@field type? datadog.v2.SensitiveDataScannerTextReplacementType|string

---Type of the replacement text. None means no replacement.
---hash means the data will be stubbed. replacement_string means that
---one can chose a text to replace the data. partial_replacement_from_beginning
---allows a user to partially replace the data from the beginning, and
---partial_replacement_from_end on the other hand, allows to replace data from
---the end.
---@alias datadog.v2.SensitiveDataScannerTextReplacementType "none"|"hash"|"replacement_string"|"partial_replacement_from_beginning"|"partial_replacement_from_end"

