---Attributes of a usage quota bulk write result. On success, quota fields are present as applicable, and pending fields are present only when a change is scheduled. On failure, only `error` is present and the other fields are omitted.
---@class datadog.v2.UsageQuotaBulkResultAttributes
---@field enforced? boolean Whether usage above the limit is actively blocked instead of only tracked or alerted on. Omitted if this item failed to write.
---@field error? string An error message describing why this item failed to write. Omitted if this item was written successfully.
---@field org_public_id? string The public ID of the organization that owns the quota. Omitted if this item failed to write.
---@field pending_effective_from? string The future UTC month when the scheduled limit takes effect, formatted as `YYYY-MM`, starting at 00:00 UTC on its first day. Present only together with `pending_usage_limit` and omitted when no change is scheduled or this item failed to write.
---@field pending_usage_limit? number The usage limit scheduled for the organization-wide quota in the usage units defined by the quota namespace. A value of `0` is valid. At the start of the effective month, this value becomes `usage_limit` and both pending fields are omitted. Omitted when no change is scheduled or this item failed to write.
---@field scope? datadog.v2.UsageQuotaResponseScope
---@field usage_limit? number The quota limit in the usage units defined by the quota namespace. May be fractional for quotas configured before public writes required whole units. Omitted if this item failed to write.

---The result of writing one usage quota in a bulk create-or-update request.
---@class datadog.v2.UsageQuotaBulkResultData
---@field attributes datadog.v2.UsageQuotaBulkResultAttributes
---@field id string An opaque usage quota identifier. Clients must pass this value back verbatim in update and delete requests and must not infer any structure from it.
---@field type datadog.v2.UsageQuotaType

---The results of writing each usage quota in a bulk create-or-update request, in the same order as the request.
---@alias datadog.v2.UsageQuotaBulkResultDataList datadog.v2.UsageQuotaBulkResultData[]

---Attributes for creating or updating a usage quota by scope. Each item must provide `usage_limit`, `pending_usage_limit`, or both. Providing only `pending_usage_limit` updates an existing organization-wide quota, never creates one, requires `enforced` to be omitted, and fails if the quota does not exist.
---@class datadog.v2.UsageQuotaCreateAttributes
---@field enforced? boolean Whether to actively block usage above `usage_limit` instead of only tracking or alerting on it. Required when `usage_limit` is provided and must be omitted when only `pending_usage_limit` is provided.
---@field pending_usage_limit? number The non-negative, whole-number limit to schedule for the organization-wide quota in the usage units defined by the quota namespace. It is not checked against current usage. Each write schedules the value for 00:00 UTC on the first day of the next calendar month and replaces any previously scheduled change; the server computes `pending_effective_from`. Omit this field to leave any scheduled change unchanged, including when raising `usage_limit`. Cancel a scheduled change only by deleting the quota's `/pending` sub-resource.
---@field scope? datadog.v2.UsageQuotaRequestScope
---@field usage_limit? number The non-negative, whole-number quota limit to set in the usage units defined by the quota namespace. For an organization-wide quota (scope omitted), the limit must be greater than usage already recorded in the current period. When this field is provided, `enforced` is required.

---A usage quota resource to create or update by scope.
