---Patch a saved filter
---
---Partially updates a saved filter. Supports both `LIST` and `RULES` filters.
---Supply at least one of `name`, `description`, or `targeting_rules`. Omitted or null fields
---are preserved. Supplying `targeting_rules` replaces the entire collection and propagates
---changes to every feature flag that references the saved filter.
---Metadata-only updates do not require edit permission or approval on those feature flags.
---Rule updates require edit permission on all consumer flags and are rejected when approval
---is required, unless the caller has the `feature_flag_approvals_override` permission.
---The optional `last_updated_at` field detects stale updates. It does not set the update time.
---
---`PATCH /api/v2/feature-flags/saved-filters/{saved_filter_id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input datadog.v2.UpdateSavedFilterAttributesRequest
---@return datadog.v2.SavedFilterResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:update_saved_filter_attributes(input) end

---Update Scanning Group
---
---Update a group, including the order of the rules.
---Rules within the group are reordered by including a rules relationship. If the rules
---relationship is present, its data section MUST contain linkages for all of the rules
---currently in the group, and MUST NOT contain any others.
---
---`PATCH /api/v2/sensitive-data-scanner/config/groups/{group_id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input datadog.v2.UpdateScanningGroupRequest
---@return datadog.v2.SensitiveDataScannerGroupUpdateResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:update_scanning_group(input) end

